cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "SaUCE: Sparse and Unbiased Clustering Estimator"
version: 0.3.2
license: MIT
url: "https://github.com/OscarHickman/SaUCE"
repository-code: "https://github.com/OscarHickman/SaUCE"
authors:
  - family-names: Hickman
    given-names: Oscar
    affiliation: "Institute for Computational Cosmology, Durham University"
    email: oscar.hickman17@alumni.imperial.ac.uk
keywords:
  - cosmology
  - galaxy clustering
  - correlation functions
  - N-body simulations
  - astronomy
abstract: >
  Correlation function counters for galaxy catalogues drawn from sparse
  subsets of periodic N-body simulations. Computes xi(r), xi(s, mu)
  multipoles, and high-order N-point functions with unbiased corrections for
  statistical under-sampling in m-of-k sparse samples.
